# E §4.2 step 5: "the legs of steps 0-2 ... together, against the balance they leave"; L §5.10: refused "with the legs
# at the place that brought it there: the batch's". p1 moves 10.00 PLN from the claim x (5.00) to the claim y (0), p2
# 20.00 PLN from y out: the batch leaves x at -5.00 PLN and y at -10.00 PLN, both broken, so p1 (at x) and p2 (at y)
# are refused. snap11 tested the places one by one in name order: x refused p1, whose refusal marked y, so p2 printed
# 20.00 PLN, and with the names swapped it would not have (writer 8, sixth pass, beside C2-1).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place x: claims PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place y: claims PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place z: outside lives 2026-01-01..
input amt: money PLN
input amt2: money PLN
input day: date

move p1: transfers
  on day
  leg cash from x to y amount amt

move p2: transfers
  on day
  leg cash from y to z amount amt2

ask q: flows(p1, 2026-03)
ask q2: flows(p2, 2026-03)

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  amt = 10.00 PLN
  amt2 = 20.00 PLN
  day = 2026-03-10
  opening[x] = 5.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  opening[y] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
=== expect
q: refused: RUN-PLACE x is -5.00 PLN after the day's observations and plans of 2026-03-10
  cut 2026-01-01
q2: refused: RUN-PLACE y is -10.00 PLN after the day's observations and plans of 2026-03-10
  cut 2026-01-01
